{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1495 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b15c3a4b7c2db02e4a7913f259d96cc9cb560d418853eab9f7d37ede97cd7e51" :edb/db-before-t 1494 :edb/db-after-t 1495 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534807 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:37:12.088Z" 13194139534807 true] [17592186100733 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311330 13194139534807 true] [17592186100733 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311342 13194139534807 true] [17592186100735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311337 13194139534807 true] [17592186100735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311348 13194139534807 true] [17592186101278 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534807 true] [17592186101278 1100 "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\csc x = 2$? Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534807 false] [17592186101278 1100 "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534807 true] [17592186101278 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arcsin}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/978eaf470ef3b61ff7839471ed4ac46f320922b4d30f7f95566095124d0526d7.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311331 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1089 "q-120782" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1113 #uuid "632e22b1-4c21-5851-8b21-7ad3340c1c1b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311330 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311332 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311333 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311334 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311335 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311336 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1041 "selection" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311336 13194139534807 true] [17592186311331 1110 #uuid "f3331e7d-006c-5595-aeaf-5ee73606601c" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311332 1034 "x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " 13194139534807 true] [17592186311332 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311332 1111 #uuid "859c250d-2b30-552d-ae3c-889d52560a8b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311333 1034 "x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " 13194139534807 true] [17592186311333 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311333 1111 #uuid "e51c143e-0228-535b-a244-e7bd8401d80b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311334 1034 "x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " 13194139534807 true] [17592186311334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311334 1111 #uuid "9f536c92-6810-58a6-9a22-b4c02c0a7b16" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311335 1034 "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " 13194139534807 true] [17592186311335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311335 1111 #uuid "80a8e54a-5ed3-528c-8cf7-ee928714cd1b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311336 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " 13194139534807 true] [17592186311336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311336 1111 #uuid "ed428b22-42d0-5407-8593-3e4394c24e8f" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311338 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311340 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1089 "q-274743" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/c21ae590fc35738a016fd9c6191bd15685d0d0a6fb043f32aafaf8d01845d149.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=2\\sqrt{3}.$\nFind an expression of the form\n$x=\\theta +n\\cdot b,$\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in radians, that generates the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1113 #uuid "a9d71686-b3e3-56dd-9035-b577ffa85e92" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311337 1145 "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\cdot \\pi .\n$$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311339 13194139534807 true] [17592186311338 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311338 1041 "field-1" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311338 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311339 13194139534807 true] [17592186311338 1110 #uuid "a0dc8136-78b1-51cd-8bb0-7981ddb1579d" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311339 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311339 1111 #uuid "c94e9d2b-284a-52d2-ba7f-baaff6fe66e0" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311341 13194139534807 true] [17592186311340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311340 1041 "field-2" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311340 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311341 13194139534807 true] [17592186311340 1110 #uuid "82d72786-5802-51bf-9552-45f2e9edc431" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311341 1034 "\\pi" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311341 1111 #uuid "d358064a-616d-5753-bcbb-bf73e5caf37c" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311343 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311346 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1089 "q-323844" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}$ in the form $x=\\theta +n\\cdot b$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{180}^{∘}),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in degrees.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that $tan\\,({157.5}^{∘})=1-\\sqrt{2}.$*\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1113 #uuid "53ae4089-fae5-5e2e-bcd5-a0d30f0a1606" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311342 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1-\\sqrt{2})={157.5}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{∘}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={157.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311344 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311345 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1041 "field-1" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311345 13194139534807 true] [17592186311343 1110 #uuid "b5635edf-d997-5eb2-9b51-363cf90d8fa5" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311344 1034 "22.5" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311344 1111 #uuid "f3bb088b-fc9e-539b-b43d-ba82676fd51e" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311345 1034 "157.5" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311345 1111 #uuid "2cff173a-6d90-5010-8f96-79a850e718d7" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311347 13194139534807 true] [17592186311346 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311346 1041 "field-2" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311346 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311347 13194139534807 true] [17592186311346 1110 #uuid "7c344193-d1ed-5d28-8299-769f411a67b6" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311347 1034 "180" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311347 1111 #uuid "e093a81d-bfff-52b5-833b-b345c9c4f6ee" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311349 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311351 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311353 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1089 "q-324057" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/435dd125850e3f97b5c3753a027f2db8718131ab499ef6711eaac637b1a022bd.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$ Find expressions of the form\n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+n\\cdot b,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+n\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ ${\\theta }_{1},{\\theta }_{2}\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ $b$ is the period in radians, and $n$ is an integer, that generate the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection.\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1113 #uuid "cedbaa79-cb49-5c7d-aff2-1b5dd0191c77" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311348 1145 "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the $2$nd quadrant and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/b0738a8a505b89ff687cb4de350a00f2e10d6209fbeee7dcdfdf0ee359a9cc3c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\text{ }{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\text{ }\\text{and}\\text{ }b=2\\pi .$" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311349 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311350 13194139534807 true] [17592186311349 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311349 1041 "field-1" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311349 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311350 13194139534807 true] [17592186311349 1110 #uuid "e7ba593a-f1f0-5418-a8eb-07e5de558f6b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311350 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311350 1111 #uuid "e4d68d7d-09fa-51cf-aa08-370f48525dd2" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311352 13194139534807 true] [17592186311351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311351 1041 "field-2" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311352 13194139534807 true] [17592186311351 1110 #uuid "c1ed9ab0-0795-5822-bb80-8f5256a23ea0" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311352 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534807 true] [17592186311352 1111 #uuid "1bd37bb4-91aa-515b-96a8-90ec14232643" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311354 13194139534807 true] [17592186311353 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534807 true] [17592186311353 1041 "field-3" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311353 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311354 13194139534807 true] [17592186311353 1110 #uuid "ce81aac1-d715-5cde-9352-1a11e1f69d4b" 13194139534807 true] [17592186311354 1034 "2\\pi" 13194139534807 true] 